  "id": "Compound::DB00139 - Gene::8974",
  "verbalization": "Succinic Acid appears to interact with multiple P3h proteins, which are involved in the proline oxygenation pathway critical for collagen synthesis. These interactions are supported by a consistent pattern across three distinct paths, each linking Succinic Acid to P4ha2 through a shared intermediate, Procollagen-proline Dioxygenase Activity. The evidence suggests that Succinic Acid may act as a substrate or modulator of these enzymes, influencing their activity and, consequently, their role in collagen formation. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential mechanism where Succinic Acid could regulate the proline oxygenation process, potentially affecting P4ha2's function. The integration of these findings implies that Succinic Acid may play a role in the biological processes associated with P4ha2, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
